      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2000219783,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "`IOG_ITEM_UNIT_CALC_THROUGHPUT` was also not added as a choice to all the `case` statements, e.g. to `hasItemToShow()` and the related `showsZero()`.\n\nThe current behavior with zeros is to omit zeros from the \"counting\" statistic scatter plots, but show them in other plots. For the calculated summary statistics, zeros are always omitted if the field didn't appear in the given intervals. (eb4e2cca69c5057995ff7d59848d784895904bb0)\n\nI'm not completely sure this is the best way to do it (also see #11694), but which way should THROUGHPUT behave? Probably like the other summary statistics, because a zero when the interval is too small isn't useful.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
